0..65 Comment "// A motive that names a path type, a bridge type or a flow type."
66..68 Comment "//"
69..146 Comment "// A motive is a function from an index to a type. Its body is a computation,"
147..223 Comment "// and a type is a value. So the body writes `return` before the type, as it"
224..292 Comment "// does before any value. The function itself is a value too, so the"
293..325 Comment "// definition returns its thunk."
326..328 Comment "//"
329..344 Comment "// - see: #6491"
